is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
The fault lies in the BIND 9 DNS server (`named`) running on **srv1** (10.5.0.4), the campus DNS server referenced in PC1's `/etc/resolv.conf`. The configuration file `/etc/bind/named.conf` — written when the lab started on 2026-08-04 — contains the directive `recursion no;` in its global options block. BIND is therefore operating in pure authoritative mode: it answers only for the single zone it owns (`jeremysitlab.com`) and returns an immediate `REFUSED` response to every recursive query for any external domain name (e.g., `google.com`). This was confirmed by `nslookup google.com 10.5.0.4` → **REFUSED**, while `nslookup srv1.jeremysitlab.com 10.5.0.4` → 10.5.0.4
